SELECT '132c625d-e876-4412-a98e-1b0229e3b570',id,user_id,'user','revision','Automated visual acceptance feedback for the current v005 CNN draft, from actual browser screenshots. The scan window and timeline repairs now pass independent checks. A remaining issue is the formula strip in scenes cnn-15-python-forward and cnn-16-python-backward: with y=627, height=26 and fontSize=18, the summation subscript u,v is still visibly clipped. At the tested viewport the foreignObject bottom is 837.840px but the subscript glyph bottom is 842.360px (the subscript group reaches843.640px), and the footer starts at839.120px. The outer KaTeX box being inside the region is insufficient: its child glyphs overflow. Move the formula strip upward and provide enough height, or reflow the panel, leaving clear space before the footer; do not merely make overflow visible into neighboring content. Recheck all math strips with actual screenshots and descendant glyph bounds, including compact viewport. Preserve the corrected scan/code/timeline behavior, the native editable context and all prior versions. Keep 20 pages. This is a visual repair; reuse the verified mathematics and code. Do not put audit details or this feedback on teaching slides.','[]','pending',CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER) * 1000,CAST(strftime('%s','now') AS INTEGER) * 1000
FROM jobs WHERE id='db69fb9d-5d27-4fc2-9553-a722e2a5acbc' AND status='running' AND user_id=(SELECT user_id FROM jobs WHERE id='2d8c4072-7aee-4f55-8fb0-8f074de4f8cb' AND title='介绍cnn')
